   7:     """Move each solid colored rectangle upward by exactly its own height.
   8: 
   9:     Input structure
  10:     A black-background grid contains one or more separated monochromatic
  11:     foreground objects. Each object is a solid axis-aligned rectangle, with an
  12:     equally sized empty region immediately above it.
  13: 
  14:     Rule
  15:     Clear every rectangle from its original position, then paste the same
  16:     rectangle directly above that position, offset upward by the rectangle's
  17:     height.
  18: 
  19:     Key insight
  20:     The vertical displacement is not shared globally: each rectangle jumps by
  21:     its own bbox height, so its new bottom edge is just above its old top edge.
  22:     """
  23:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  24:     bg = get_bg(g)
  25:     comps = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)
  26:     assert comps, "expected at least one foreground rectangle"
